        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0662" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10958: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-03T16:00:00+08:00">November 3, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 3—9:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>886. 1. Representatives here of the former Communist troops (Eighth Route New
                    Army) are reported as stating a second army of former Communist troops from
                    Fukien, Kiangsi and other places is being organized at Hankow to be known as the
                    Fourth Route New Army.</p>
                <p>2. Li Tsung Jen is at present in Nanking. Kwangsi troops on the Tsinpu front are
                    understood to be second and third line troops and not the best of the Kwangsi
                    forces.</p>
                <p>3. From information reported by hospitals caring for wounded soldiers, it is
                    stated that Chinese wounded at present total 150,000 of <pb facs="0663" n="656"
                        xml:id="pg656"/> which 50,000 are in the north. The number killed is
                    variously estimated at one to every 3, 2 or 1 wounded.</p>
                <p>4. Repeated to Peiping, Hankow, Shanghai, Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
